  "Question": "Susan had \\(\\$50\\) to spend at the carnival. She spent \\(\\$12\\) on food and twice as much on rides. How many dollars did she have left to spend?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 12 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 14 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 26 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 38 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 50 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Twice the \\(12\\) dollars spent on food is \\(2\\cdot12=24\\) dollars spent on rides. Subtract both expenses from Susan's \\(50\\) dollars:\n\\[\n50-12-24=14.\n\\]\nShe has \\(\\boxed{14}\\) dollars left, choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
